  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e965f9168c2046c28c59aa4b83cc1ec, type: 3}
  m_Name: CooperativeBox
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-cooperativebox
  DisplayIndex: 16
  DisplayName: Two to escape
  Shape: 15
  TeachingHint: Hold cyan A to let B cross. B presses amber to release A. Get BOTH
    balls out.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 3375090899389237206, guid: 1c04a19ca1c7c4aa5b6b7f9d665cbd52, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: Two steel balls share one rotating box and Earth gravity. Cyan
    A holds a spring plunger while amber B crosses the right gate. B then compresses
    the retaining plunger, which holds both powered shutters open. Retrieve A from
    its holding pocket and guide both spheres to the one round exit. Shutters remain
    physical colliders throughout their motion. The level only completes after both
    full spheres have left. Shared exit assist pulls the ball through an unobstructed
    opening within 40 mm. This is deliberate gameplay assistance; the entire sphere
    must still physically clear the bore before completion.
